## Worksheet

**F1 (Core loop):** state G/S single object; mulberry32 rnd(S) used for every random call (no Math.random); endTurn() executes steps 1-10 in fixed order. Score 2.

**F2 (Map):** genMap() builds 8x8 via rnd(S); canBuild() checks B.terr.includes(t.ter); adjMult() multiplies real output in outputMult(). Score 2.

**F3 (Economy):** mine→ore, forge consumes ore+power→metal, workshop consumes metal→parts; cap() clamps + logs overflow each turn. Score 2.

**F4 (Population):** addColonist() creates skill/fatigue/morale/job/assigned; outputMult() reads c.skill and c.fatigue. Score 2.

**F5 (Needs):** needF/needW consumed in endTurn step3; shortage cuts c.morale; morale feeds outputMult; morale/fatigue regenerate when no shortage/resting. Score 2.

**F6 (Research):** 10 nodes; doResearch() enforces R.pre and deducts cost; each unlock read in outputMult/cap/needs/storm-chance/price/canBuild. Score 2.

**F7 (Events):** 12 EVENTS entries; weighted roll via pool.reduce(w)+roll loop; 5 events (refugees, sickness, cache, contam, lostcaravan) offer 2-3 differing-outcome choices; S.eventCd cooldown checked in pool filter. Score 2.

**F8 (Trade):** price() reads S.res[g]/cap and S.drift[g] (drifts each turn); S.caravan.inv limited and decremented; trade() handles buy & sell. Score 2.

**F9 (Hazard):** storm every STORM_EVERY turns, sev grows with S.turn; damaged tiles skip production (`if(t.damaged)continue`); stormwalls/windbreak reduce chance; repair() costs 2 parts + engineer. Score 2.

**F10 (Save/load):** serialize() to textarea; validateLoad() parses/validates fields, shows saveerr on bad input. Score 2.

**F11 (End conditions):** win (turn>60,pop>=12,food&water>0) and lose (col.length===0) both reachable; score() sums pop/research/stock/turn/winBonus; renderOver() shows summary modal. Score 2.

**F12 (UI):** switchTab()/TABS wiring; log lines show T${l.t}; tooltips via data-tt/resTip/outputMult breakdown; Space/1-6 keydown handler; @media(max-width:420px) rule. Score 2.

**F13 (Dev panel):** runTests() asserts real invariants (cap respected, determinism hash equality, save/load round-trip, assignment uniqueness); runBenchmark() runs 200 headless greedyStep turns and prints hashState(). Score 2.

**G1:** research flags (filtration/hydroponics/smelting/logistics/rationing/stormwalls) read in outputMult()/cap()/needs/storm-chance every relevant turn, visible via tooltip. Score 4.

**G2:** shortF/shortW (step3) → c.morale -=10/-12 (step4) → outputMult() multiplies output by morale tier next production tick. Score 4.

**G3:** ashstorm sets t.damaged=true → production loop `continue`s damaged tiles (zero output) → repair() spends 2 parts, clears damaged, restoring output. Score 4.

**G4:** price() = BASEPRICE×S.drift[g]×stockF(S.res[g]/cap); drift updates every turn in step8. Score 4.

**G5:** refugees/sickness/contam/lostcaravan choice branches write S.res, S.col morale/fatigue/assigned directly, not just log(). Score 4.

